// ============================================================================
// Activation flag bit assignments (DEC-85)
// ============================================================================
// Sixteen bits, 0..15, live in unit+0x3A/0x3B. Give a bit to a skill with one
// of the two macros below; each bit may be owned by exactly one skill ID.
//
//   ActivationFlagOncePerTurn(SkillID, bit)
//     Scope byte 0. Cleared for every unit at the top of each player phase.
//
//   ActivationFlagOncePerMap(SkillID, bit)
//     Scope byte 1. Cleared only when the unit is loaded, i.e. when the
//     chapter starts and everything else resets.
//
// To retire a skill, delete or comment out its macro line below and free its
// row in the table. A skill left at SKILL_OFF still burns its bit, so do not
// leave assignments in place for skills you are no longer using.
//
// The ID column is the value skill_definitions.event resolves the name to --
// it is what lands in SkillActivationFlagTable, and what you would look for
// in a RAM watch on unit+0x3A. tests/test_skill_activation_flags.py checks
// this table against the macro calls below, so it cannot drift.
//
// bit | skill      | ID  | scope
// ----+------------+-----+---------------
//   0 | Hurricane  |   4 | once per turn
//   1 | (free)     |   - |
//   2 | (free)     |   - |
//   3 | (free)     |   - |
//   4 | (free)     |   - |
//   5 | (free)     |   - |
//   6 | (free)     |   - |
//   7 | (free)     |   - |
//   8 | (free)     |   - |
//   9 | (free)     |   - |
//  10 | (free)     |   - |
//  11 | (free)     |   - |
//  12 | (free)     |   - |
//  13 | (free)     |   - |
//  14 | (free)     |   - |
//  15 | (free)     |   - |
//
// Bits 0-7 are byte 0x3A, bits 8-15 are byte 0x3B.
//
// Example of the other scope:
// ActivationFlagOncePerMap(MiracleID, 1)

ActivationFlagOncePerTurn(HurricaneID, 0)
